ng — it is that the trail and the ladder are two exits competing for the same lots, and the trail wins 58% of the time on the lot the ladder was designed to let run. ·  The number: 231 sessions: rung fill rates 71.0% / 39.4% / 11.3% / 4.8%; all four rungs net negative; lot 4 closes on the trail 133 times and on its $600 rung 11 times. Live since 08-20: four entries, sixteen lots, exactly ONE rung has ever filled (the $100 lot on 08-25). ·  Proven wrong by: Re-run <code>scripts/rev2_rider_stop_231.py</code> with the rung mix logged per lot and confirm the four fill rates. Live: count TARGET_100/200/400/600 exit reasons in <code>trades</code> against rider entries.</div></details><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
