<div class="pk-card" id="p-mgc-depth-mid-bars-0821" data-id="mgc-depth-mid-bars-0821" data-default="live" data-pick="1"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">BUILD #1 · Movement 3 §8 (gold, in its own right); the MGC dossier §3 and §12.1 in the appendix. · ★ Build the depth-mid bar source into the MGC shadow — the gating item for all of gold</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Point the MGC shadow service&#x27;s minute-bar builder at the <strong>depth mid</strong> instead of at trades, and keep the existing trade-bar arms alive as <code>*_tradebar</code> controls so the difference is visible rather than asserted. Nothing else on the gold line is worth doing first.</div><div class="pk-meta">Last week&#x27;s shadowed gold gate has been live since Monday and is losing: <strong>−$1,196 across 80 trades in seven days, all three arms red</strong>. The lab replay of the same seven days makes +$512.</div><details class="pk-det"><summary>why &amp; the full detail</summary><div class="pk-more-why">The cause is the input tape: the research builds one-minute bars from the depth mid (which updates every 250ms whether or not anything trades), the service builds them from trades, and gold prints sparsely — so a sixty-minute high on one is not the sixty-minute high on the other. Hold everything else constant and change only the tape: depth-mid bars n=56 → <strong>+$172 (+$3.06/tr)</strong>; trade bars n=53 → <strong>−$475 (−$8.96/tr)</strong>. The sign flips on the bar source alone. ·  This is a plumbing mismatch between lab and production, not a research failure, and the fix is mechanical: the service already holds a <code>DepthFeed</code> connection to gold&#x27;s book because the liquidity filter needs it, so it already has the bid and the ask. Until it lands, no gold cell should be promoted and none is being proposed. ·  The number: Live shadow −$1,196 / 80 trades vs lab +$512 on the same days. Bar-source A/B on the six days both tapes cover: +$3.06/tr vs −$8.96/tr. ·  Proven wrong by: Both arms present in <code>data/shadow_mgc.db</code> under distinct names, and a week of forward trades where the depth-mid arm and the <code>*_tradebar</code> control diverge in the predicted direction.</div></details><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" id="p-shadowvariant-missing-fields-0821" data-id="shadowvariant-missing-fields-0821" data-default="live" data-pick="1"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">BUILD #2 · Movement 3 §9 item 5; the RIDER_ALL dossier §11 in the appendix, which lists all three blockers with the one-line fix for each. · Add atr_min, a wrapping clock window and an ER10 gate param to ShadowVariant</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Three small changes to <code>src/gazbot7/shadow.py</code>: (1) <code>gate_board</code>&#x27;s window test becomes <code>inw = (lo &amp;lt;= h &amp;lt; hi) if lo &amp;lt; hi else (h &amp;gt;= lo or h &amp;lt; hi)</code> so a 21:00→07:00 window can exist at all; (2) <code>ShadowVariant</code> gains an <code>atr_min</code>, defaulted to 0.0 so nothing existing changes; (3) an <code>er_win_min</code> that reads the ENTRY WINDOW&#x27;s efficiency rather than ER30.</div><div class="pk-meta">All three are blockers on shadowing anything from this movement honestly. A rule that is a BAND cannot be expressed with only a ceiling.</div><details class="pk-det"><summary>why &amp; the full detail</summary><div class="pk-more-why">A wrapping clock window is never true, so an overnight arm silently never fires. And <code>ShadowVariant.er_min</code> reads ER30 — substituting it for the 10-minute ER FLIPS the held-out leg from +$5.34 to −$2.25 a trade and turns both controls positive, i.e. it is a different hypothesis wearing the same name. ·  ★ This is exactly how <code>rider_w5</code> came to be quoted at +$19.29 while making −$28.84. An arm shipped AROUND a missing field records a different strategy under the intended name, and nothing downstream can tell. ·  The number: ER30 substituted for ER10 flips the held-out leg +$5.34/tr → −$2.25/tr and reverses both controls. ·  Proven wrong by: A unit test that an arm with <code>hh_lo=21, hh_hi=7</code> fires at 23:00Z and not at 12:00Z, and one that <code>atr_min</code> excludes a below-band fire.</div></details><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
