<div class="pk-card" id="p-census-vocabulary-0821" data-id="census-vocabulary-0821" data-default="shadow" data-pick="1"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">BUILD #4 · Movement 3 §4; the FLOW-LED, UNCLASS and OPEN-NEWS dossiers in the appendix each reach it independently. · ★ Rename two census labels, stop splitting on flow, and ship the four run SHAPES</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Three edits to the census&#x27;s vocabulary: <code>UNCLASS</code> → <code>UNTESTED</code> and report it as COVERAGE; <code>OPEN/NEWS</code> → <code>US-OPEN-WINDOW</code> with the two footprint tests DELETED; stop splitting runs into <code>FLOW-LED</code>/<code>VACUUM</code> at all. Then add the four run SHAPES — TURN, STEP-REPRICE, DRIFT-VOID, GRIND-CONT — one <code>if</code> each, all computable at the run&#x27;s start minute.</div><div class="pk-meta">Three of the five labels were interrogated directly this week and none survived. <code>UNCLASS</code>: base rate 75.4% on all tape, lift <strong>0.82</strong> — a run is LESS likely to be UNCLASS than an arbitrary minute is.</div><details class="pk-det"><summary>why &amp; the full detail</summary><div class="pk-more-why"><code>OPEN/NEWS</code>: lift over the bare clock <strong>0.921×</strong>, i.e. the two footprint tests remove 41% of the window and keep the LESS run-dense half. <code>FLOW-LED</code>/<code>VACUUM</code>: the flow event fires on 20.4–20.6% of all tape and then splits it on a <strong>49.6–49.9% coin toss</strong> — 0.33 percentage points of directional information. ·  These are independent measurements by different hunts on different tape, and two of them are the second such measurement in two weeks. The vocabulary is the thing the whole cold half of the report is scoped by; leaving it wrong is more expensive than any single gate on this card. ·  The number: UNCLASS lift 0.82 on 75.4% base; OPEN/NEWS lift 0.921× over the bare clock; FLOW-LED/VACUUM split carries 0.33pp. Replacement: <code>VOL-EXPANSION</code> is <strong>4.18× lift on 1.95% of tape</strong> and the census barely uses it. ·  Proven wrong by: Next week&#x27;s census prints the new names and a <code>VOL-EXPANSION</code> bucket with more than one member.</div></details><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
